{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1zWS5jPgu5ciKHWUKM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YLiPJWMyBae22qtMTimYDB","name":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-WvDwDg && sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/' gen.py && python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | grep -c '\"start\"'\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# HR corridors clamped to watch zones\n\n## Change\n`gen.py` `hr_target()` now emits `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}` instead of `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n\n## Why\nThe readback (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`) shows we sent `value`/`end`. The API accepted it (steps populated), so the problem was not rejection. Per the colleague's note, the key name for the lower bound selects the FIT export mode. `value`+`end` becomes a zone-mapped Lap-HR target, which the watch clamps to its own zones. `start`+`end` becomes an Instant-HR corridor, which shows the raw bpm Intervals computes (% x Intervals LTHR 172). That matches the watch-notes symptoms: every step showed a watch zone band, and changing the watch LTHR moved the bands but they stayed zone edges.\n\n## Colleague's note: what applied\n- Applied: `value` -> `start`, keeping `%lthr` units. This is the only change.\n- Already consistent: we use percentages, not bpm. `units: \"bpm\"` and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` were already ruled out in watch-notes.\n- Not applied: the top-level `description` text grammar. Our readback shows `workout_doc.steps` populated and the notes don't report a web-UI problem. I left it alone.\n\n## Not verified\nI couldn't push or sync a watch, so the expected watch result is untested: 68-75 -> ~117-129 bpm, 88-93 -> 151-160, 75-82 -> 129-141, 65-72 -> 112-124. Please push a test event, read it back and check the watch. Also confirm that the readback shows `start`, since the API could normalise it.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"contain